            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="JOH03" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Henry Erskine</forename>
                        <surname>Johnston</surname>
                        <addName>Hendry</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1775-08-03">
                        <placeName>Scotland</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1845-02-08"/>
                    <occupation>actor</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Johnston was regaled as the Scottish Roscius after immediate success on the Edinburgh stage in 1794. He made his London debut as Norval in John Home's 
   <title>Douglas</title> in October 1797 which prompted Godwin to write to him with both praise and advice.</p>
                        <p>The Johnston entry for 2 November 1797 has been coded as Henry as it is probable that he called on Godwin in response to the letter but other instances of 
    Johnston have not been so coded due to lack of evidence.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 55, fols. 28-30: 24 October 1797</bibl>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 22, fol. 70: 24 October 1797</bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
